## Data sources

CaiJing Today is a **reader**. It ships the schema it reads
([`docs/SCHEMA.sql`](docs/SCHEMA.sql)) and a synthetic demo dataset
([`docs/samples/demo_data.sql`](docs/samples/demo_data.sql)); it ships no
scraper and no snapshot of real market data.

The `source` values the feed carries — `akshare_em_global`,
`akshare_em_cjzc`, `gdelt`, `polygon`, `rss`, `sec_edgar` — name the kind of
upstream a collector would have read them from. They are a published
vocabulary, not bundled data. If you connect a collector of your own and
redistribute what it produces, **you** are responsible for complying with the
terms of every source it read, and with the rights in the headlines and
summaries it collected. Nothing in this repository grants you any right to
real financial news content.

The demo dataset is entirely synthetic: no real headline, quote, index level,
percentage move, economic-calendar entry or URL appears in it. Instrument
names are real because they are the taxonomy the UI renders against; every
value attached to them is invented. See the header of
[`docs/samples/demo_data.sql`](docs/samples/demo_data.sql) for the full rules.

